## Mastery gate

You are ready to move on only after you can:

- explain **Rehashing and Load Factor** without looking at notes;
- implement the core operation in C;
- dry-run one unseen case;
- identify at least two failure modes;
- justify time and auxiliary space;
- complete the independent practice;
- solve or at least meaningfully attempt a relevant LeetCode transfer problem.

### Transfer rule
Do not memorize a LeetCode solution. Map the problem back to the underlying university concept: representation → invariant → operation → proof → complexity.


---
### Further learning & visual reference
- **GeeksforGeeks / C-DSA:** https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/c/learn-dsa-in-c/
- **W3Schools / C:** https://www.w3schools.com/c/
- **AlgoTutor:** https://www.algotutor.io/mastering-dsa-system-design
- **Programiz / C:** https://www.programiz.com/c-programming
- **VisuAlgo / visualization:** https://visualgo.net/en/sorting

